  "note": "Same-scope independent rejudgment of the complete RFC 4271 Section 9.1.2 sentence: a change of either the immediate next hop or the IGP cost to NEXT_HOP requires Phase 2 selection again. Read all six tagged covers, their actual unit and daemon fixtures, the production Loc-RIB subscriber, forked metric revision/cache worker, extraction, ranking and mirroring paths, the retained record cuts and the renewed negative receipt. The immediate-hop unit drains initial and no-op extraction observations before changing only the interior gateway at fixed cost 10. It requires a new production candidate lookup against that gateway, resolution true, unchanged received BGP NEXT_HOP and no AIGP. The positive fault removes immediate-hop change detection in Path.Equal. The renewed negative fault corrupts only the mirrored received NEXT_HOP; its accepted clean run passes, while its observed mismatch is the initial learned-address preservation assertion at line 101. That is an honest preservation control, not a separately observed post-change failure. The cost-only unit isolates equal earlier BGP attributes without AIGP, arranges the cheaper route against the later address tie-breaker, changes only interior cost A10 to A30 to A5, and requires selected Loc-RIB A to B to A without another UPDATE or a direct selector call. Its retained subscriber cut preserves initial selection and fails the first required cost-driven move to B. The retained-input unit additionally asserts initial preference, reachable fallback after one cover disappears, absence after both disappear, retention of received paths and restoration without UPDATE. Its selection-trigger cut and each ordinary internal/forked CI selection-trigger cut preserve initial selection and fail after interior-cover change. Both real-socket daemon placements retain their unchanged BGP-best, Loc-RIB, exact all-table kernel and direct-control lifecycle assertions; authenticated placement and successful queries are required. Forked revision changes clear ordinary and prospective caches before retained-route reselection. These carriers do not separately prove cost-only or immediate-gateway-only daemon/kernel behavior. The old CIs gained only an additional 3.1-2 tag; no old tag, input, assertion or lifecycle stage was removed. Read the accepted renewed initial-preservation diagnostic and independently parsed the final native freshness report: all six covers are current, with zero stale and zero unproven records. Exact clean assertions cover both mandatory triggers and the feasible preservation control; no assertion or claim was weakened to renew the record. A discrimination record is confined to its observed primary failure, not proof that every later recovery assertion ran under its fault. The bound production and fixture/helper inventory preserves those meanings. No broader ranking, packet-forwarding or new prospective-integration claim is made by this rejudgment.",
